This migration tree owns only the PostgreSQL research-chat schema. The legacy
SQLite document and drafting metadata remains separate and is not migrated.

Configure these environment variables in backend/.env before connecting:

    POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
    POSTGRES_PORT=5432
    POSTGRES_USER=lankalawbot
    POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<development-or-secret-manager-value>
    POSTGRES_DB=lankalawbot
    POSTGRES_POOL_SIZE=10
    POSTGRES_MAX_OVERFLOW=5
    POSTGRES_AUTO_CREATE_SCHEMA=false

Keep ``POSTGRES_AUTO_CREATE_SCHEMA=false`` in production. Application startup
then verifies PostgreSQL connectivity and expects the versioned migrations to
already be applied. Set it to ``true`` only for an explicit local/test bootstrap.

For local development, start the isolated PostgreSQL service from the backend
directory after setting POSTGRES_PASSWORD in your shell:

    docker compose -f docker-compose.postgres.yml up -d

From the backend directory, apply migrations with:

    alembic upgrade head

Generate future revisions only after importing all conversation models into
alembic/env.py:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe schema change"

The legacy SQLite metadata database is intentionally outside this migration
tree.

Do not call init_postgres() during a production startup. It is an explicit
local/test bootstrap helper; production schema changes must go through Alembic.
